/target
**/*.rs.bk
.DS_Store

# Python bytecode from the hook pack. Committed by accident once: the hooks
# are stdlib-only scripts, so a .pyc is pure build output and a stale one
# shadows a source edit in a copied tree, which is how a mutation run reports a
# green suite against code it did not actually run.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# cargo-mutants campaign output. `tests/publication.rs` reads the working tree
# through `git ls-files --cached --others --exclude-standard`, so an un-ignored
# campaign is PUBLISHED as far as every grammar in that file is concerned — and
# its logs carry real wall-clock instants, which is exactly what the timestamp
# gate exists to refuse. Measured: one scoped run left 307 files under the root
# and `every_record_timestamp_is_an_allowlisted_fixture` failed.
#
# The gate is right and the artefact is simply not publishable, so the fix
# belongs here rather than in an allowlist. Narrow on purpose: three names this
# one tool writes, never a pattern that could swallow a real file. `mutants.out`
# is unanchored because it is the directory cargo-mutants creates inside
# whatever `--output` it is given; the other two are the repository-root paths
# `.github/workflows/mutants.yml` writes.
/mutants-run/
/mutants.log
mutants.out/
